WRITTEN ARGUMENTS ON BEHALF OF THE ACCUSED

RESPECTFULLY SUBMITTED:

I. AGE OF VICTIM

The most critical issue in this case is the age of the victim. The prosecution claims the victim is 15 years old based on a school certificate. However, this certificate is unreliable and refers to a different person with the same name. The school records are not properly authenticated.

II. OSSIFICATION TEST

The ossification test conducted by the medical board gives an age range of 16-18 years. This is inconclusive and does not definitively establish that the victim is a minor. The test has a margin of error of ±2 years.

III. BIRTH CERTIFICATE

The prosecution has failed to produce the birth certificate of the victim, which is the most reliable document for age determination. Its absence raises serious doubts about the claimed age.

IV. CONSENSUAL RELATIONSHIP

Even assuming the victim is a minor, the relationship was consensual. There is no evidence of force, threat, or intimidation. The victim attended tuition voluntarily and maintained contact with the applicant.

V. POSITION OF TRUST

The prosecution alleges that the applicant was in a position of trust as a tuition teacher. However, the applicant was not a regular teacher but provided private tuition. The position of trust argument is overstretched.

VI. MANDATORY REPORTING

The fact that the incident was reported within 24 hours shows that there was no attempt to conceal the alleged offence. This supports the applicant's case of innocence.

VII. PRIOR CONDUCT

The applicant has been a tuition teacher for 10 years with no complaints whatsoever. He has a clean record and is respected in the community.

VIII. LEGAL POSITION

The Supreme Court has held that in cases where age is disputed, the court must carefully examine all evidence. The prosecution has failed to prove beyond reasonable doubt that the victim is a minor.

IX. BAIL PRINCIPLES

The applicant is not a flight risk. He has deep roots in the community. There is no likelihood of tampering with evidence. The trial is likely to take a long time.

PRAYER

It is therefore prayed that the applicant be granted bail and the charge under POCSO Act be reconsidered in light of the age determination issues.

